content:
A membership of Northgate Memberships whose tier allows a mid-year upgrade is moved to its Plus counterpart on the upgrade date, the expiry date does not move, and the upgrade fee is charged that day to the tender the member chooses.

## Prerequisite clause

The upgrade fee is fixed only after the membership stands active with a renewal or new membership fee for its current membership year recorded on the membership ledger.

## What the upgrade write records

Member services records the upgrade. One call:

- changes the tier on the membership to the stated Plus tier;
- leaves the membership number and the expiry date unchanged;
- records the upgrade fee on the membership ledger as an upgrade difference charge for the membership year currently on the membership, billed to the stated tender.

The member sees the new tier on the membership from that day.

## Invocation

The tool is `upgrade_membership_to_plus_9f256f7b`, an agent-side tool: member services unlocks it and then calls it.

## Parameters

| Parameter | Meaning | Format |
|---|---|---|
| `membership_id` | the membership reference number of the membership being upgraded, as returned by the membership lookup | identifier |
| `upgrade_tier` | the official tier the membership moves to | one of the six tier names below, exactly |
| `upgrade_fee` | the upgrade fee charged | USD with 2 decimal places, always positive; stored rounded half up to 2 decimal places as passed, with no tax added |
| `tender` | how the upgrade fee is paid | one of the tender codes below |

`upgrade_tier` takes exactly one of:
  - Northgate Student Club Membership — the discounted student tier, kept only while the student verification is valid;
  - Northgate Heroes Club Membership — the discounted military and first-responder tier, kept only while the service verification is valid;
  - Northgate Club Membership — the standard consumer tier, also the tier a lapsed Student Club or Heroes Club renewal converts to;
  - Northgate Business Membership — the standard business tier held in a licensed business name;
  - Northgate Club Plus Membership — the consumer Plus tier that earns Annual Reward;
  - Northgate Business Plus Membership — the business Plus tier that earns Annual Reward.

`tender` takes exactly one of:
  - `cash_or_debit` — paid from a debit card or cash at a counter;
  - `northgate_visa` — charged to the member's Northgate Rewards Visa card;
  - `northgate_store_card` — charged to the member's Northgate Store Card;
  - `other_credit_card` — charged to any other credit card the member names;
  - `shop_card` — paid from a Northgate Shop Card balance;
  - `reward_certificate` — paid with an Annual Reward certificate;
  - `not_applicable` — never used for a payment, only for entries that carry no payment.

## Return

A text receipt reading "Upgrade recorded", followed by the upgrade entry reference on the membership ledger, the membership reference, the new tier, the fee charged in USD with 2 decimals, the tender, and the unchanged expiry date (YYYY-MM-DD). A receipt starting "Upgrade recorded" means the tier change and the fee are both on the membership.

## Points of reference

- *Does the expiry date move?* No; the membership keeps its expiry date and membership number.
- *Which tender is billed?* The tender the member chooses.
